<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="072" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>GET /api/v1/records/{table}/{id}/family — own endpoint file, ledger + census, uniform 404 (FR-31)</title>
    <phase>7 W7 Record family service and Family tool</phase>
    <gate>071 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New BFF endpoint (auth required); route-authorization ledger; existence-equalised 404.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Thin endpoint over 071's reader following the existing /api/v1/records group pattern; the security logic lives in 071.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W7-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Builds on 071.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>071</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, endpoints, auth, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add `GET /api/v1/records/{table}/{id}/family` in a new file `Api/Records/RecordFamilyEndpoints.cs`, in the existing `/api/v1/records` group, calling `RecordFamilyReader`; register it in the route-authorization ledger and the governed-file census.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, ProblemDetails, route-authorization guards.</role>
  <goal>A caller can fetch a record's Filing family as specified in FR-31; an unknown and an unreadable anchor are indistinguishable; the route is governed by the existing authorization guards.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-31; design.md §12.3 C (UAC F2: own file, ledger, census; T2: the anchor in the 404). `RecordNoAccessEndpoint.cs` stays one cohesive No Access responsibility (§11.5) — do not add the route there.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Records/RecordFamilyEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/RecordNoAccessEndpoint.cs (the /api/v1/records group and its auth)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs (ledger entry with mechanism)</file>
      <file role="modify">the governed-file census test that lists endpoint files (re-grep "census")</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Program.cs or the module that maps the records group (one Map call)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Api/Records/RecordFamilyEndpointsTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-31">Query: kind (default Filing; any other value → 400 before any probe), direction (default full; `down` accepted; anything else → 400), continuation (opaque).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-31">Response: anchor, optional root, truncated, continuation, members[] each with id, table, name, recordNumber, recordType, status, modifiedOn, kind, edgeKind, parentId, depth. No access metadata.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-31 (contract pinned 2026-10-27 for task 073)">`anchor` and `root` are `{ id, table, name }` (name nullable). `depth` is a non-negative integer counted down from the top of the view the caller can read (the highest readable ancestor = 0; the anchor's own depth follows from that). The client `RecordFamilyModal` (073, `recordFamilyService.ts` `asRef`) already parses exactly this; keep property names camelCase as listed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-31 / #2137">Unknown and unreadable anchor → the same 404 ProblemDetails, via the equalised gate probe (timing equalised).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / root §9">Auth required; route registered in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger with its mechanism; census updated.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Errors are ProblemDetails with fixed text; detail to logs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Placement Justification; publish-size delta; CVE check.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare FULL rigor; confirm 071 is merged.</step>
    <step order="1">Write the contract tests first; confirm they fail.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the endpoint file, map it in the records group, add the ledger and census entries.</step>
    <step order="3">Run the filtered suites and ArchTests; publish size; CVE check.</step>
    <step order="4">Update TASK-INDEX.md to ✅ [done]; notes in notes/task-072-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>The /api/v1/records group (RecordNoAccessEndpoint.cs) — extended with a new route in its own file.</existing>
    <extension>The group is extended; the route gets its own file so RecordNoAccessEndpoint.cs keeps one responsibility (§11.5).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The TrackingFieldTrio Family tool and the ribbon have no way to list a record's family.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Records/RecordFamilyEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/domain/Api/Records/RecordFamilyEndpointsTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">200 with the documented shape for a readable anchor; members carry kind and edgeKind; root omitted when not readable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unknown anchor and unreadable anchor return the identical 404 body via the equalised probe.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">kind≠Filing and an invalid direction each return 400 before any probe or Dataverse call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An unauthenticated call is 401; the route appears in the ledger with its mechanism and in the census (ArchTests green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An invalid or tampered continuation returns the same 400 as a malformed one.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the contract cases above only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build 0 errors; filtered suites and ArchTests green; publish-size delta and CVE recorded.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
